<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγνύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ύος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἡ</span> (parox. in <i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			1.57
		</span></i> P.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thick smoke mixed
				with flame, murky fire</i> (such as is made by burning resinous
			substances, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				387b6
			</span></i>, al.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱέντα . . διὰ στόμα λιγνὺν μέλαιναν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					494
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέροψ λ.</span>, of the fires
			seen by night on the two peaks of Parnassus, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1127
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. σῶμα καταιθαλοῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1241
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. καὶ καπνός</span> Id. 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Lys.</u>
				319
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγνὺς πρόσεδρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					794
				</span></i>
			, expld. by Sch. of the <i>smoke</i> of the altar hanging
			round Heracles: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ φλόγες καὶ αἱ λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					34.11.18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.2.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>soot</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐστι καπνώδης
			αἰθάλη</span> Erot.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλῶσσαλιγνυώδης</span>
			; used medicinally, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.61
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				322
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i> l.c., and prob. in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
			</span></i> l.c.]</div>
